+      # `method_exists($obj, $name)` bounds a subsequent dynamic method call `$obj->$name()` to the
+      # DECLARED methods of a concrete object — i.e. not arbitrary code execution. This is the standard
+      # guarded-dispatch idiom (`if (method_exists($o,$m)) { $o->$m(...); }`); without it the
+      # code-injection query reports every such call as RCE (the dominant dynamic-dispatch FP class:
+      # er24-rechtstexte, t3-cat-search, femanager setters, …). NOT is_callable/function_exists — those
+      # are true for `system`/`exec`, so they do not bound the callee.
